{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1's system clock to synchronize with pool.ntp.org.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The persistent timesyncd drop-in explicitly sets NTP=pool.ntp.org. Direct observations before and after reboot show pool.ntp.org as the live server, NTP enabled, the clock synchronized, and a received synchronization packet.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6a18aa0300f0468e","cmd-5303992ba19644a5","cmd-cb6ea52328554184"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep time synchronization active and recover it across system restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy pre-restart baseline showed the service enabled, active, and synchronized. The reboot was acknowledged, connectivity was interrupted, and node1 returned with a different boot ID. Synchronization was initially pending after boot, then recovered to an active, synchronized pool.ntp.org session, demonstrating the complete restart transition.","evidence_ids":["cmd-665090c306aa4e5b","cmd-6d11f1bfa377467b","cmd-23034d19ae3744f1","cmd-55ffcec915644aff","cmd-93b8af6b5d764735","cmd-86248f4fa8ec4bda","cmd-cb6ea52328554184","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The only intentional state changes were creating the required persistent timesyncd configuration, enabling/restarting its service, and scheduling the required reboot; each directly supported a task outcome or restart verification. The failed ssh.service existed before execution and remained unchanged, package health stayed intact, and socket and temporary-file differences are ordinary reboot/runtime changes rather than harmful residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6a18aa0300f0468e","cmd-6c3e2cd29f4b4fb2","cmd-6d11f1bfa377467b","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied. The restart protocol strongly establishes an acknowledged reboot, independently corroborated boot-ID change, persisted configuration, recovered service, and restored live synchronization with pool.ntp.org.","limitations":["The restart evidence demonstrates task-service health but not a globally healthy systemd state: node1 reported degraded immediately before disconnect and after reboot, while lifecycle snapshots show this was caused by a pre-existing ssh.service failure that remained unchanged. This does not reduce task functionality but modestly limits provider-wide restart evidence quality. Evidence: cmd-22a9565535cb4962, cmd-55ffcec915644aff, global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services, global:after_executor:node1:failed-services."]}
